what happened overnight is being called  reckless by some european officials the  u.s embassy in ukraine is calling it a  war crime while the ukrainian president  is calling it nuclear terrorism  according to the ukrainian military  russian forces attacked and eventually  seized the facility surveillance camera  footage appears to show russian  artillery shells being fired at the  plant there are also images of a flare  lighting up the area there was a fire in  a building it was extinguished that  building is apparently used for training  and not a part of the plant that  generates power now the ukrainian  company that runs the country's four  nuclear power plants says although  russian forces are now in control the  staff is still working the company  however is not in communication with  them nuclear experts say active warfare  around nuclear power plants is something  the world should be concerned about  this is our worst nightmare come true  you know this is a  europe's biggest power power plant six  reactors  if it goes offline if we have nuclear  meltdown among six reactors this is  gonna be worse than chernobyl  the company says three ukrainian  soldiers were killed in the fight over  the plant two were injured  the russian defense ministry claims  ukrainian saboteurs would have provoked  the fighting meantime nato's secretary  general says the russian attack on the  plant shows the recklessness of this war  and the importance of ending it  mike armstrong global news cheshire  poland
 

